0221: draws skipped for a missing pipeline are logged; shadow casters wait for their pipeline

Every draw dropped because its pipeline is missing (creation failed, LM_PIPELINE_WAIT=0) or still
compiling (shadow casters, until now) is counted. A warning line "N draws skipped for a missing
pipeline in the last x s (k shadow casters)" goes to the log every second with a non-zero count, and
the first skip of each pipeline is logged once with its config: the MISS detail, recorded when a
draw asks for a pipeline that is not built yet, whether it is precached or not ("precache list
entry" when no draw asked for it). It is always on. resolve_pipeline clears its thread-local
config pointers after the lookup, because miss_detail() now always runs. Light shadow-map casters (render_casters)
took their pipeline with try_get_pipeline and skipped the draw while it compiled, so that light had
no shadow in that present. They now wait like every other draw (patch 0013 policy). Motivation: a
user capture under 100% CPU load showed a candle light alternating between shadowed and
unshadowed presents (docs/INTERPOLATION.md "Foyer entry flicker report").

